-### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-- **Negative $Q_v$ Components:** If any component of $Q_v$ is negative, the ray originates outside the cube or points away from the relevant face, yielding no valid entry/exit within the box bounds defined by the logic [S1, unofficial].
-- **All Negative $Q_v$:** If all components of $Q_v$ are negative, the ray does not intersect the cube in the forward direction [S1, unofficial].
-- **Division by Zero:** If `raydir[i]` is 0, the division results in infinity or NaN [S1, unofficial].
-- **Precision:** Clamping the intersection point to the exact boundary (`dir_lower` or `dir_upper`) is critical to avoid self-intersection artifacts in subsequent traversal steps [S1, unofficial].
 
